RESP {"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"capabilities":{"prompts":{"listChanged":false},"resources":{"listChanged":false,"subscribe":false},"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"instructions":"ACOS exposes an agent-oriented Android verification API. Start with acos_help (the full agent guide: loop, CLI examples, scenario YAML, error playbook, limits) and acos_capabilities for what is implemented. The core loop is inspect -> verify -> read the verdict -> fix -> rerun. `unsupported` means the engine cannot do it: never rewrite the app to hide it, never call it a pass. `fail` means the app ran and a check did not hold: read the assertion diff. Tool results are the ACOS JSON envelope; `isError` is true whenever status != pass.","protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","serverInfo":{"name":"acos-mcp","version":"0.3.0"}}}
