ys written to `tree_path`; a full tree over the reply cap is replaced by the compact view and the path.","type":"boolean"},"include_frame":{"default":true,"description":"Include frame metadata.","type":"boolean"},"max_nodes":{"description":"Maximum nodes to return (truncation is reported).","format":"uint","minimum":0.0,"type":["integer","null"]},"png":{"default":false,"description":"Capture this frame's PNG into the reply (`true`).\n\nThe ART daemon writes it under the session's artifacts and reports the path (same as `screenshot: true`); the Flutter route returns the PNG inline (`png_base64`/`png_bytes`). A route that cannot produce pixels answers `UNSUPPORTED_BACKEND` instead of a reply that silently has none.","type":"boolean"},"screenshot":{"description":"Write this frame's PNG (`true` = under the session's artifacts and return the path; a string = that destination inside the artifacts directory).\n\nThe pixels are always those of the frame the tree in the same reply describes; a placeholder/no-pixel frame is `NO_FRESH_FRAME`, never an empty success.","type":["boolean","string"]},"session_id":{"description":"Session to address, the same value as `base.session_id` (the documented short form: `acos_observe_tree {\"session_id\": \"mcp-1234\", \"screenshot\": true}`). Omit it for this server process's default session.","type":"string"},"settle_timeout_ms":{"description":"P12b: bound this verb's strict/fast settle wait. On timeout the reply still carries the latest tree and frame identity with `settled:false` and `bound:timeout`; a timeout is never assertion evidence.","maximum":600000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"text":{"default":false,"description":"Include the newline-joined text rendering.","type":"boolean"},"tree":{"default":true,"description":"Include the structured UI tree.","type":"boolean"}},"required":["base"],"title":"ObserveRequest","type":"object"},"name":"acos_observe","title":"acos observe"},{"_meta":{"acos":{"available":true,"command":"action","fid